{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1094", "sample_idx": 9, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "```json\n{\n  \"famous_moms\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Lady Bird Johnson\",\n      \"also_known_as\": \"The First Lady Who Turned Roses Into a National Obsession (and a Total Plant Lady)\",\n      \"claim_to_fame\": \"She made America love wildflowers so much that groovy, flower-power kids of the '60s started calling her 'The Rose Lady'—until she just went and planted them everywhere, including the White House lawn like it was her personal garden party.\",\n      \"fun_fact\": \"She survived a plane crash in 1942, married LBJ, and still had time to host the most stylish White House parties. Icon.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Patti Smith\",\n      \"also_known_as\": \"The Rockstar Poet Who Raised a Kid While Smashing Glass (Literally and Figuratively)\",\n      \"claim_to_fame\": \"She gave birth to Jesse Paris Smith in 1979 while her punk-rock band was still going strong, then proceeded to write *Witt* (a novel about motherhood) and *August Rock* (a memoir where she kicks ass and takes names). Also, she once headbutted a TV during a performance—kids, take note.\",\n      \"fun_fact\": \"She’s the only mom ever to be called 'the punk poet laureate' by a very confused but awed audience.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Jada Pinkett Smith\",\n      \"also_known_as\": \"The Will & Grace Mom Who Also Runs a Beauty Empire (and Probably a Secret Book Club)\",\n      \"claim_to_fame\": \"She’s been a mom to Willow and Harper while producing *Will & Grace*, starring in *The Matrix Resurrections*, and somehow still has time to launch her own skincare line. Also, she’s survived alopecia, remarried famously, and still makes time for a good wig collection.\",\n      \"fun_fact\": \"She once said, 'I don’t have a lot of patience for people who don’t take care of themselves.' Mic drop.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Mayim Bialik\",\n    